    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0628" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg548"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Lord
                            Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2330.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note, No. 3, of the 2d instant, and to inform you in reply that
                    I have made known to the Secretary of the Treasury that the government of Canada
                    concurs in the suggestion that the practice of flying flags over the
                    custom-houses of the United States in Canada and of Canada in the United States
                    be discontinued, and I suggested that the Treasury Department’s officers
                    stationed in Canada be instructed in that sense.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
